{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">Failing the build on every axe violation blocks unrelated PRs on pre-existing issues until someone disables the check entirely — and then it catches nothing at all.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Record a baseline of known violations (rule id plus selector), then diff future runs against it — fail CI only on violations a PR actually introduces.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Allowlist specific instances, not whole rules, exclude third-party subtrees you don't control instead of disabling rules sitewide, and track the baseline's size on a dashboard so it burns down instead of quietly growing.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
